# The vendored tree is verified byte-for-byte against the SHA-256 digests in
# each crate's `.cargo-checksum.json`. Any end-of-line translation on checkout
# — which git does by default on Windows when `core.autocrlf=true` — rewrites
# those bytes and every build then dies with "checksum mismatch".
#
# `-text` disables EOL translation for the whole repo, so a Windows checkout is
# byte-identical to a Linux one.
* -text
